  "term": "obsessive-compulsive personality disorder",
  "definition": "Obsessive-compulsive personality disorder is a mental or behavioral disorder marked by a lasting pattern of rigidity, extreme orderliness, and perfectionism that gets in the way of being efficient. It can affect many areas of life, including work, leisure, finances, and questions of morality or ethics.",
